In ncurses windows,

There should be a backend buffer containing the text displayed (containing the decorations (ansi codes, etc)).

This buffer has L lines and C columns (maximum length of line).

The window in which it's displayed has H lines and W columns.

When L>H or C>W to see the whole buffer we must scroll.

There's a scrolling point (Sl Sc) which indicates the first line and first columns displayed in the topleft corner of the windows.

These commands apply only on the active windows.

| key   | alt key | alt key 2  | description   | command             |
|-------+---------+------------+---------------+---------------------|
| C-w > | C-x >   | C-<prior>  | increments Sc | window-scroll-right |
| C-w > | C-x <   | C-<next>   | decrements Sc | window-scroll-left  |
| C-w v | C-v     | <kp-next>  | increments Sl | window-scroll-up    |
| C-w ^ | M-v     | <kp-prior> | decrement Sl  | window-scroll-down  |

Prefix C-u N let us specify the number of lines or columns to increment or decrement.
Otherwise some default value is used.
Scrolling is bound to the current backend text size minus the current window size.
If one or the other changes, the next scrolling command may skip to adjust Sl or Sc.

Let's add a key / command to display the key bindings:

| key   | description              | command           |
|-------+--------------------------+-------------------|
| C-h m | Display key binding help | help-key-bindings |

Note: for window commands, let's add:

| key   | alt key | description                            | command      |
|-------+---------+----------------------------------------+--------------|
| C-w o | C-x o   | swap active window between two windows | window-other |

window-other uses a saved active window initialized to nil

When the saved active window is nil, then save the current active
window, and activates the next-window.

When the saved active window is not nil, then activates the saved
active window, and reset it to nil.


For other window commands, with a C-w something key binding, let's add a C-x something key binding.
